    {
      "id": "claim_17f1263b05e84c63a2703b683d80a395",
      "statement": "MotionMatchingDataVisualiser draws a baked database's poses and the trajectory features extracted from them, so a feature pointing the wrong way — the usual cause of a search picking odd frames — is visible there and nowhere else, before any synthesis is involved.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Debugging/Visualisers/MotionMatchingDataVisualiser.cs#L10-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2b9a7c5e369a96493564514f885015070f4f00d81a5bd0f927cbb4d8286bda50:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_657609c6d82d4413851799e32148c2c6",
      "statement": "PoseSetVisualizerStage plays a pose database straight through with no search and no control input, which is how an import, an extraction or a retarget is inspected with the rest of the pipeline out of the way.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Pose/PoseSetVisualizerStage.cs#L8-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9a422c589d62982d7ad0dd49d6004d785e7fc468521d4e913028f9a20047e043:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9ba32f66205f43359bef014f531f6337",
      "statement": "ContactVisualizerStage applies the same velocity-threshold test the pose extractor uses when baking contacts, but against the pose the whole pipeline produced after searching and blending — so it answers whether a foot is planted right now rather than which frames a future bake would mark.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Core/ContactVisualizerStage.cs#L11-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c13202b30b274d49981e02862a21e8d95f74e346b21a661cdb8ad068041116d9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1baa4c2bc8e342fa8b02c304223fbb9b",
      "statement": "The contact visualizer carries a private pose buffer in its own layout, adding one bool channel per configured bone, because the pipeline's layout only carries the two built-in foot contacts and a read-only stage must not change the layout everything else shares.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/MotionMatching/Runtime/Core/ContactVisualizerStage.cs#L36-L48",
